@risks

  - instance bindings break on move (mitigation: S2 repoint BEFORE commit,
    bindings-valid green required)
  - manifest dest stale after moves (mitigation: doc_manifest rescan)
  - write-gates block legacy files touched (mitigation: normalize to
    1.2.1 at transition, same as S5 record normalization)
  - archival = data-loss risk (mitigation: moves only, git history,
    archive dir inside workspace — R17 respected)

@decision_needed_S5

  D-A: archive destination — docs/archive/<cycle>-<ts>/ (chosen here) or
       a second frozen snapshot like spec_revision?
  D-B: normalization scope — only files touched by sweeps (chosen) or
       full 430-file legacy normalization now?
  D-C: experiment .py — stay with records (chosen default) or scripts/?
  D-D: execute both circles now, or lifecycle-docs first and pause?

